    {
      "id": "cta-13",
      "type": "cta",
      "content": {
        "image": {
          "src": "https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6465c08bc2eb8d26649eade8/65b97c9b5f7173ae2730ec92_TotalPollution_act2.jpg",
          "alt": ""
        },
        "heading": "Sign The Petition",
        "text": "People everywhere are rising up in resistance against the fossil fuel industry. The industry is built on colonialism and injustice. From systemic pollution and environmental damage to displacement of communities, murder, fraud, misleading greenwashing marketing campaigns and now the global energy crisis.\n\nLET'S END FOSSIL FUEL CRIMES AGAINST HUMANITY AND THE CLIMATE.",
        "button": {
          "label": "Act To End Fossil Crimes",
          "href": "#"
        }
      },
      "overrides": {
        "size": "big"
      },
      "overrideReasons": {
        "size": "as on the live site (phase 1)"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "text-14",
      "type": "text",
      "content": {
        "heading": "Production",
        "body": "The CG of TotalPollution was produced under the expert guidance of VFX supervisor Tim Smit. The production commenced early May and took 3 months to complete. A faithful replica of Stade de France was created, where, just like in the film, the first game of the Rugby World Cup will be played between France and New Zealand on September 8th, 2023. The stadium was then populated with a crowd of 80,000 mannequins and 2 rugby teams.\n\n‍\n\nThe biggest challenge were the massive oil simulations that had to dynamically interact with the crowds and players. Some of the simulations contained North of 1.5 billion voxels (3D pixels), which required lots of computing power and patience. Through very precise planning and digital storyboarding the team was able to complete these massive simulations within the deadline and with a very minimal crew.\n\n‍\n\n**Watch the BTS film by Redivider Studio below!**\n\n‍"
      },
      "padTop": "4-5",
      "padBottom": "4-5"
    },
